%%{init: {'theme': 'base', 'themeVariables': { 'primaryColor': '#4285F4'}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    participant User as "User"
    participant App as "Mobile/Web App"
    participant Firebase as "Firebase Auth"
    participant Backend as "Backend Server"
    participant Firestore as "Firestore"

    Note over User,App: 1. User initiates login

    User->>App: Enter credentials<br/>(phone/email/password)
    App->>Firebase: Authenticate()

    Note over Firebase: Verify credentials<br/>Generate ID token
    Firebase-->>App: Firebase ID Token<br/>(JWT)

    Note over App,Backend: 2. API request with token

    App->>Backend: GET /api/resource<br/>Authorization: Bearer <token>

    Note over Backend: 3. Token verification

    Backend->>Firebase: verifyIdToken(token)
    Firebase-->>Backend: Decoded Token<br/>{uid, email, ...}

    Note over Backend: 4. Role verification

    alt User is Admin
        Backend->>Firestore: Query admins<br/>WHERE firebaseUid == uid
        Firestore-->>Backend: Admin profile found
        Backend->>Backend: Set role = admin
    else User is Employee
        Backend->>Firestore: Query employees<br/>WHERE firebaseUid == uid
        Firestore-->>Backend: Employee profile found
        Backend->>Backend: Set role = employee
    else User is Customer
        Backend->>Firestore: Query customers<br/>WHERE firebaseUid == uid
        Firestore-->>Backend: Customer profile found
        Backend->>Backend: Set role = customer
    else Not Authorized
        Backend-->>App: 403 Forbidden
    end

    Note over Backend: 5. Process request

    alt Authorized
        Backend->>Firestore: Query/Write data
        Firestore-->>Backend: Response
        Backend-->>App: 200 OK + Data
    end

    Note over App: 6. App handles response

    App->>App: Update state<br/>Store token<br/>Navigate to home